{{ 'dev-contact-form.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- comment -%} Fixed design tokens from Figma — not merchant-controlled {%- endcomment -%}
<style>
  .dev-contact-form {

    --font-title-size: 32px;
    --font-title-size-mobile: 24px;
    --font-heading-weight: 500;
    --font-heading-lh: 1.2;

    --font-body-size: 18px;
    --font-field-size: 16px;
    --font-body-weight: 500;
    --font-body-lh: 1.4;
    --font-button-weight: 700;

    --card-radius: 32px;
    --card-pad: 32px;
    --card-pad-mobile: 24px;
    --card-gap: 16px;

    {%- comment -%} Phone line (owner, 2026-09-25). 24px between the email line and the phone — the low end of
       the requested 24–32px, and the same 24px the mobile stack already uses (--stack-gap-mobile),
       so desktop and mobile show the same space. The card's own 16px gap is subtracted in the CSS.
       Number in the site's brand green (the footer logo's #4EA448) and underlined, as the mockup
       draws it; hours one step down at 16px. {%- endcomment -%}
    --phone-gap: 24px;
    --phone-icon: 24px;
    --phone-icon-gap: 12px;
    --font-hours-size: 16px;

    {%- comment -%} Fluid, not stepped. A single breakpoint at 1024 left 1025–1200 holding the full 533px card
       AND the full 136px gutter, so the form was squeezed to ~228px at 1025 — the worst point on
       the curve sat just ABOVE the breakpoint meant to fix it. The vw terms are the artboard ratios
       (64/1440, 136/1440, 533/1440), so at 1440 they resolve to exactly 64 / 136 / 533 and the pixel
       reference is untouched; below that everything scales together. {%- endcomment -%}
    --section-px: clamp(24px, 4.4444vw, 64px);
    --section-py: 40px;
    --col-gap: clamp(40px, 9.4444vw, 136px);
    --card-w: clamp(280px, 37.0139vw, 533px);

    {%- comment -%} The 1440 artboard less its two 64px insets. Above 1440 the vw terms above have all hit
       their max, so without this cap the card and gutter would freeze at 533/136 and the form
       column alone would absorb every extra pixel of viewport. {%- endcomment -%}
    --container-max: 1312px;

    --section-px-mobile: 16px;
    --section-py-mobile: 16px;
    --stack-gap-mobile: 24px;

    {%- comment -%} The Figma "Input Fields" component exposes no layout of its own, so these are measured off
       the 1:1 render (45246:3826): 58px tall, 1px #666666 stroke, transparent fill, text 18px from
       the top edge and 20px from the left. Radius fitted to the corner arc — 4px, NOT the footer
       input's 8px.

       The padding is short of those insets ON PURPOSE. Figma draws a stroke INSIDE the box, so its
       padding is measured from the outer edge. CSS puts the border OUTSIDE the padding, so
       border + padding must add up to the Figma inset. Using the inset directly makes every field
       2px too big and shifts the text 1px.

       And the block padding is 16.8, not 17. The real inset is not a round 18: a 58px box holding a
       16px/1.4 line (22.4px) leaves (58 - 22.4) / 2 = 17.8px a side. Rounding that to 18 left the
       content box 0.4px shorter than its own line, and a textarea whose content overflows by any
       amount grows a scrollbar — visible even when the field is empty. 1 + 16.8 = 17.8 makes the
       line fit exactly, and the scrollbar goes away at the root instead of being hidden. {%- endcomment -%}
    --field-h: 58px;
    --field-pad: 16.8px 19px;
    --field-radius: 4px;
    --field-border-w: 1px;

    --field-gap: 8px;
    --form-gap: 16px;

    {%- comment -%} Same inside-stroke correction: the button is 148x46 with a 1px white stroke and its label
       12px/18px from the outer edge, so 1 + 11 = 12 and 1 + 17 = 18. {%- endcomment -%}
    --button-pad: 11px 17px;
    --button-radius: 60px;
    --button-border-w: 1px;

    {%- comment -%} The Figma fill is a translucent dark neutral, not a solid: #343434 at 66%. Fixed, like every
       other button on the site — no section lets a merchant recolour one, and this one used to be
       the exception with three settings for it. {%- endcomment -%}
    --button-bg: rgba(52, 52, 52, 0.66);
    --button-color: #ffffff;
  }
</style>

{%- comment -%}
  Contact. 45246:3640 (desktop) / 45246:1199 (mobile).

  Desktop: cream card on the left (sticky), the form on the right.
  Mobile:  the card becomes a full-width banner holding ONLY the centred heading, and its body
           copy drops out of the card to sit underneath it as plain copy — then the form.

  That reflow is done with `display: contents` on the card at <=768 rather than by rendering
  the copy twice. Duplicating it would put the same paragraph in the DOM twice, which screen
  readers and search engines both read as two paragraphs.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div
  class="dev-contact-form"
  style="
    --bg: {{ section.settings.background_color }};
    --color: {{ section.settings.text_color }};
    --card-bg: {{ section.settings.card_color }};
    --field-border: {{ section.settings.field_border_color }};
    --field-border-hover: {{ section.settings.field_border_hover_color }};
    --field-placeholder: {{ section.settings.placeholder_color }};
    --accent: {{ section.settings.phone_color }};
    --pt: {{ section.settings.padding_top }}px;
    --pb: {{ section.settings.padding_bottom }}px;
  "
>
  <div class="dev-contact-form__inner">
    <div class="dev-contact-form__card">
      {%- if section.settings.title != blank -%}
        {%- comment -%} inline_richtext: already safe HTML from Shopify — never escape it. {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          <h1>, not <h2>. This section IS the page's main content — the page templates render no
          title of their own, so before this the whole document had no h1 at all and its outline
          opened at level 2. The children below are h2 for the same reason: an h1 followed by an h3
          is a skipped level.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <h1 class="dev-contact-form__title">{{ section.settings.title }}</h1>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if section.settings.body != blank -%}
        <div class="dev-contact-form__body">{{ section.settings.body }}</div>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        Phone line under the email (owner, 2026-09-25): a clear 24–32px space above it, the number
        as a tap-to-call link, the opening hours on the line below. Number and hours are THEME
        settings (Theme settings -> Contact details), shared with the footer so the two can never
        disagree; the tel: link comes from snippets/dev-phone-href.liquid.

        Inside the card on desktop. On mobile the card is display:contents (see the header note),
        so this becomes its own row under the intro copy — the 24px row gap there IS the space the
        owner asked for, no extra margin needed.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if settings.contact_phone != blank and section.settings.show_phone -%}
        <div class="dev-contact-form__phone">
          <svg class="dev-contact-form__phone-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
            <path d="M3 5C3 3.89543 3.89543 3 5 3H8.27924C8.70967 3 9.09181 3.27543 9.22792 3.68377L10.7257 8.17721C10.8831 8.64932 10.6694 9.16531 10.2243 9.38787L7.96701 10.5165C9.06925 12.9612 11.0388 14.9308 13.4835 16.033L14.6121 13.7757C14.8347 13.3306 15.3507 13.1169 15.8228 13.2743L20.3162 14.7721C20.7246 14.9082 21 15.2903 21 15.7208V19C21 20.1046 20.1046 21 19 21H18C9.71573 21 3 14.2843 3 6V5Z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          </svg>
          <div class="dev-contact-form__phone-text">
            <a class="dev-contact-form__phone-link" href="{%- render 'dev-phone-href', number: settings.contact_phone -%}">
              {{- settings.contact_phone | escape -}}
            </a>
            {%- if settings.contact_phone_hours != blank -%}
              <span class="dev-contact-form__phone-hours">{{ settings.contact_phone_hours | escape }}</span>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    <div class="dev-contact-form__col">
      {%- form 'contact', class: 'dev-contact-form__form' -%}
        {%- if form.posted_successfully? -%}
          <p class="dev-contact-form__success" role="status">
            {{- section.settings.success_text | escape -}}
          </p>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if form.errors -%}
          <div class="dev-contact-form__errors" role="alert">
            {{ form.errors | default_errors }}
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}

        <div class="dev-contact-form__fields">
          <div class="dev-contact-form__row">
            <div class="dev-contact-form__field">
              <label class="dev-contact-form__label" for="contact-name">
                {{- section.settings.name_placeholder | escape -}}
              </label>
              <input
                id="contact-name"
                class="dev-contact-form__input"
                type="text"
                name="contact[name]"
                value="{{ form.name }}"
                placeholder="{{ section.settings.name_placeholder | escape }}"
                autocomplete="name"
              >
            </div>

            <div class="dev-contact-form__field">
              <label class="dev-contact-form__label" for="contact-email">
                {{- section.settings.email_placeholder | escape -}}
              </label>
              <input
                id="contact-email"
                class="dev-contact-form__input"
                type="email"
                name="contact[email]"
                value="{{ form.email }}"
                placeholder="{{ section.settings.email_placeholder | escape }}"
                autocomplete="email"
                autocorrect="off"
                autocapitalize="off"
                spellcheck="false"
                required
              >
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="dev-contact-form__field">
            <label class="dev-contact-form__label" for="contact-body">
              {{- section.settings.message_placeholder | escape -}}
            </label>
            <textarea
              id="contact-body"
              class="dev-contact-form__input dev-contact-form__input--textarea"
              name="contact[body]"
              placeholder="{{ section.settings.message_placeholder | escape }}"
              required
            >{{ form.body }}</textarea>
          </div>
        </div>

        {%- render 'dev-button', variant: 'ghost', type: 'submit', label: section.settings.button_label, class: 'dev-contact-form__button' -%}
      {%- endform -%}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Contact form",
  "tag": "section",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "header", "content": "Content" },
    { "type": "inline_richtext", "id": "title", "label": "Title", "default": "Contact Form" },
    { "type": "richtext", "id": "body", "label": "Intro copy", "default": "<p>Need a hand? Send us a message and someone from our team will help.</p>" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "name_placeholder", "label": "Name field label", "default": "Your name" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "email_placeholder", "label": "Email field label", "default": "Your email" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "message_placeholder", "label": "Message field label", "default": "Your message" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "button_label", "label": "Button label", "default": "Send message" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "success_text", "label": "Success message", "default": "Thanks — we’ll be in touch shortly." },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_phone",
      "label": "Show phone number",
      "info": "The number and opening hours are set once for the whole site in Theme settings → Contact details.",
      "default": true
    },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Colors" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "background_color", "label": "Background", "default": "#FFFCF4" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "text_color", "label": "Text color", "default": "#333333" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "card_color", "label": "Card background", "default": "#FCF5E3" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "field_border_color", "label": "Field border", "default": "#D8D1C0" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "field_border_hover_color", "label": "Field border (hover / focus)", "default": "#666666" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "placeholder_color", "label": "Placeholder text", "default": "#666666" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "phone_color", "label": "Phone number", "default": "#4EA448" },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Spacing" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "padding_top", "min": 0, "max": 120, "step": 4, "unit": "px", "label": "Padding top", "default": 0 },
    { "type": "range", "id": "padding_bottom", "min": 0, "max": 120, "step": 4, "unit": "px", "label": "Padding bottom", "default": 0 }
  ],
  "presets": [
    { "name": "Contact form" }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
